Freezing the compressor (training only the decoder's low-rank adapter, the "LoRA") costs 1 to 3.5 points of judge accuracy on every eval set, at both seeds. Under the campaign's gate rules that counts as a tie, not a pass or a fail. So I launched the third-seed pair (seed 44) that the rules call for.

## Done this wake
All 20 chained jobs finished with exit 0. Each set has 1,500 questions. Each difference compares the same questions answered by both models, with a 95% confidence interval:

| eval set | frozen − reference, seed 42 | seed 43 | reading |
|---|---|---|---|
| documents | −.028 [−.049, −.007] | −.035 [−.057, −.014] | frozen is worse at both seeds |
| photos | −.009 [−.026, +.008] | −.013 [−.030, +.004] | no clear difference |
| MRQA text | −.023 [−.040, −.008] | −.027 [−.043, −.009] | frozen is worse at both seeds |
| HotpotQA (reported only, does not decide) | −.028 | −.023 | frozen is worse |

- **Why it is a tie:**
  - "Validated" needs no loss beyond 2 points on any deciding set. Documents and MRQA miss that at both seeds.
  - "Failed" needs a loss of 3 points or more, clearly below zero, at both seeds on one set. Documents at seed 42 is −2.8.
- **The loss is spread out:** every data source loses a little. None gains.
- **The freeze held:** after the full runs, no compressor or connector weight changed (0.0%).
- **Training cost:** frozen training takes 71–76 seconds per step against 90–113 for the reference.
- **Unit tests:** they now pass on committed code (12, 33 and 5 tests).

## Running now
- Seed-44 frozen finetune: ends around 03:50.
- Seed-44 reference finetune (trains everything): ends around 08:00.
- Their document evals are queued to start when each run ends.
- Both seed-44 configs differ from the seed-43 runs only in the seed.

## Next
- **In about 30 minutes:** the next wake queues the six missing seed-44 evals (photos, MRQA, HotpotQA). This wake hit its limit of six submissions.
- **What seed 44 can decide:** the frozen setup can no longer pass. It fails if seed 44 documents again lose 3 points or more, clearly below zero. Otherwise it stays a tie, and I will write you a blocked-question note.
